# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with an idle keepalive.
#
# The harness runs the image CMD so services actually boot. The CMD is
# PID-1-safe:
#   * sshd + WinRM are started first;
#   * the backdoor scheduled task is registered via schtasks.exe /Create
#     (owned by the Task Scheduler service, NOT PID 1);
#   * PID 1 is an idle `while ($true) { Start-Sleep 60 }` loop.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the malicious scheduled task is ALREADY
# registered, so a fix must delete the task (and its payload); no process runs
# as PID 1 that a restart could kill.
